      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2003 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Chronic total occlusions remain a challenge to interventionalists due to failure of crossing or perforation by strong wires. We describe the use of a system using optical coherence reflectometry for navigation and radiofrequency ablation to enable wire passage through occlusions that could not be crossed by conventional guidewires."
      },
